cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project FLAMING SWORD: Find, queue, fix, prove and land a sweep of one codebase."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  FLAMING SWORD is a code quality sweep tool that finds, queues, fixes,
  proves, and lands a sweep of one codebase. It provides six tools:
  sword (main sweep), defender (defense), sentinel (THE REAPER),
  memory_bridge (THE GRIMOIRE), chain_server (chain), and housekeep (maintenance).
  The sweep is stdlib-only and depends on nothing but the standard library and git.
authors:
  - name: "Project FLAMING SWORD contributors"
keywords:
  - static analysis
  - code quality
  - code sweep
  - automated repair
  - open source
  - developer tools
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Project CRADLE"
    notes: "Sibling project that orchestrates FLAMING SWORD's four parts."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_CRADLE"